From 6f473407ffdc96014cd28f607da17dc0bf974b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: repro-up <repro-up@local>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:58:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Make optional backends (mosek/theseus/sparseqr) optional
 and add SCS backend

Upstream commit cb3aed2 could not be run on a machine without a Mosek license:
SDPPoseEstimator hard-coded SDPRLayerMosek and sdprlayers/__init__ eagerly
imported cert_tools (module-scope 'import mosek') and theseus (module-scope
import chain theseus -> torchlie -> sksparse/CHOLMOD).  Additionally the
'solver' argument of tune_stereo_params_sdpr was accepted but silently ignored.

Changes:
* sdprlayers/__init__.py: import essential/fundamental-matrix layers and
  LieOptPoseEstimator lazily via module __getattr__ (clear ImportError on use).
* sdprlayers/layers/sdprlayer.py: 'import sparseqr' is optional; the module
  never used sqr, but the import required SuiteSparseQR headers.
* sdprlayers/layers/pose_est.py: SDPPoseEstimator(..., solver="MOSEK"|"SCS",
  scs_eps=1e-9). MOSEK default preserves upstream behaviour; SCS goes through
  diffcp/cvxpylayers (paper Sec. VI-B4 used SCS eps=1e-9).
* sdprlayers/utils/stereo_tuner.py: forward 'solver' to SDPPoseEstimator and
  import theseus lazily inside build_theseus_layer().
